<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH CROWN FIXED AT 19.500/MARK, 33.083/DOLLAR.</title>
<headline>CZECH CROWN FIXED AT 19.500/MARK, 33.083/DOLLAR.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech National Bank (CNB) fixed the crown at 19.500 to the mark and 33.082 to the dollar on Tuesday after fixing it at 18.078 to the mark and 30.475 to the dollar on Monday.</p>
<p>The central bank abolished a mark/dollar basket the crown had been pegged and said its fixing would follow the market and was only a reference point for the wider public.</p>
